VS Code Setup:
Step 1 — Install:
You need:

    1.VS Code
    2.JDK
    3.Git
    4.MySQL
    5.Node.js
    6.Maven

Step 2 — Check Java:
    Open VS Code → Terminal and type:
    java -version
    Then:
    javac -version

Step 3 — Check Git:
    git --version

Step 4 — Create project folder:
    mkdir hospital-bed-availability-system
    cd hospital-bed-availability-system

Step 5 — Open in VS Code:
    code .

Connect VS Code to GitHub:
     After creating the GitHub repository:
     git init
     Then:
     git add .
     Commit:
     git commit -m "Initial project setup"

Connect your GitHub repository:

     git remote add origin YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
     Then:
     git branch -M main
     git push -u origin main

     After this, your project will be available in your GitHub repository.

